Welcome to USING_PART3.

Here you will find basic usage information for C0rewing.

---------------- First Login ----------------

  Log in as root / root.

  Change the password immediately:

    passwd

  Add a regular user (recommended):

    useradd -m -G wheel -s /bin/bash username
    passwd username

---------------- Network ----------------

  Internet drivers are included out of the box.

  Check your connection:

    ip a
    ping -c 3 1.1.1.1

  If you do not have an IP address, you may need to start DHCP manually:

    dhcpcd

---------------- Desktop ----------------

  C0rewing uses Fluxbox as its window manager.

  Xorg starts automatically on boot via xinit.

  Default Fluxbox menu: right-click on the desktop.

  Fluxbox config: /root/.fluxbox/

  To start X manually (if it is not running):

    startx


---------------- Terminal ----------------

  tmux is pre-installed for terminal multiplexing.

  htop is available for process monitoring.

  fastfetch shows system information.

---------------- Easter Eggs ----------------

  cmatrix - digital rain effect.
  aafire  - ASCII art burning fire.

  Just run them in the terminal.

---------------- Troubleshooting ----------------

  If the system fails to boot:

    - Check GRUB installation.
    - Verify the disk is selected in BIOS/UEFI.
    - Reinstall rootfs if necessary.

  If Xorg fails to start:

    - Check /var/log/Xorg.0.log
    - Verify i915 driver is loaded: lsmod | grep i915

  If you have no internet:

    - Run dhcpcd manually.
    - Check that the interface is up: ip link set eth0 up

---------------- Notes ----------------

  C0rewing is a minimal system.
  It contains only the basic set of utilities.

  Drivers are currently only for i915 (Intel HD Graphics).
  Other hardware may require kernel recompilation.

  Some test files may remain in the rootfs.
  They can be safely deleted.

  For more information, see the repository:
  https://github.com/w1ngd3vvv/c0rewing
